description:
Implement message thread view in app.js: fetch messages for the selected chat and render them chronologically.

What: When a chat is selected, call Message/query then Message/get, render thread with sender, body, timestamp.

Algorithm:
1. async function fetchMessages(chatId):
   - const responses = await callJmap([
       ['Message/query', { accountId: 'a-self', filter: { chatId }, calculateTotal: false }, 'q0'],
       ['Message/get', { accountId: 'a-self', '#ids': { resultOf: 'q0', name: 'Message/query', path: '/ids' } }, 'g0']
     ]);
   - const [, queryResult] = responses[0]; const [, getResult] = responses[1];
   - if (queryResult.type || getResult.type) throw new Error('Message fetch failed');
   - return getResult.list;  // array of Message objects; server returns in query order
   - Store message state token: messageState = getResult.state;
2. function getSenderLabel(msg, contacts):
   - if (msg.senderId === 'self') return 'Me';
   - const c = contacts.find(c => c.id === msg.senderId);
   - return c ? getContactName(c) : msg.senderId;
3. function renderThread(messages, contacts):
   - const div = document.getElementById('message-thread');
   - div.innerHTML = '';
   - for each msg in messages (chronological order, oldest first):
     - const bubble = document.createElement('div');
     - bubble.className = 'message ' + (msg.senderId === 'self' ? 'self' : 'peer');
     - const body = document.createElement('p');
     - body.textContent = msg.body;  // CRITICAL: textContent NOT innerHTML — prevents XSS
     - const meta = document.createElement('div');
     - meta.className = 'message-meta';
     - const ts = new Date(msg.receivedAt).toLocaleTimeString();  // use receivedAt NOT sentAt
     - meta.textContent = getSenderLabel(msg, contacts) + ' · ' + ts;
     - bubble.appendChild(body); bubble.appendChild(meta);
     - div.appendChild(bubble);
   - div.scrollTop = div.scrollHeight;  // scroll to bottom

Defensive programming rules:
- MUST use textContent for msg.body — never innerHTML — XSS prevention.
- Use msg.receivedAt for timestamps (trusted server clock), not msg.sentAt (peer clock).
- msg.senderId is an opaque ID — never parse or format.
- Handle empty message list (show empty thread area, not an error).
- Message order from Message/query is query order — render as-is.

Tests (oracle: known Message object shape from JMAP spec + kith-core Message struct):
- Given msg {senderId:'self', body:'Hello', receivedAt:'2026-01-01T12:00:00Z'}, renders with class 'self' and textContent 'Hello'
- Given msg {senderId:'uid-bob', body:'Hi', receivedAt:'2026-01-01T12:01:00Z'}, renders with class 'peer'
- Given msg {body:'<script>alert(1)</script>'}, body is rendered as literal text, not executed
- Messages appear in chronological order (oldest first)
